ldren":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+4\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["20\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Military"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Military"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Colossal (Frigate) or Larger\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["20,000 (Base)\n"]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["A basic level of armor exists in all ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships"},"- it's a necessary part of building a hull strong enough to survive the rigors of space- and Starship Armor never has to be completely replaced, just patched up. However, it's possible to add additional armor beyond what's needed to keep a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"}," intact while traveling through hyperspace, and doing so can boost a ship's chance of making it out of a firefight.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Additional Starship Armor is heavy and generally obvious, giving a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"}," a blocky, military appearance. Starship Armor is bought as an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Equipment"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Equipment","referenceId":"reference:7f2465ac7cefab27"}," bonus to the Armor a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"}," adds to its ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},". Skilled pilots often prefer ships without heavy armor, since they can use their Character Level in place of a ship's Armor bonus in any case.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
